libfabric: never deliver the notification of a transfer that failed on the initiator

With 0002 the target learns when a notified transfer failed on the initiator, but it still delivered the notification
once the writes that did go out had landed (only warning that the data is incomplete), so a partly written transfer
looked complete. SGLang's KV transfers post no notification, but SGLang-Neuron's PP seam posts one with each
stage-boundary hop and needs it to mean the hop landed. The target now drops such a notification and logs an error.
The initiator reports the failure only after every request of the transfer has completed, so no write is still posted
when the entry is dropped; the application sees the failure on the initiator's transfer handle (the PP seam's sender
sees its WRITE fail and tells the receiver).

Upstream: not proposed yet (the defect is in release/1.5.0 and main)
Tests: none in this patch

diff --git a/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp b/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
index 79b0cc25..cd22aa01 100644
--- a/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/libfabric/libfabric_backend.cpp
@@ -2275,11 +2275,19 @@ nixlLibfabricEngine::checkPendingNotifications() {
                        << it->second.expected_completions;
 
             if (it->second.xfer_failed) {
-                NIXL_WARN << "Releasing the notification for notif_xfer_id="
-                          << it->second.notif_xfer_id
-                          << " whose transfer failed on the initiator; only "
-                          << it->second.received_completions
-                          << " writes arrived, so the data for this transfer is incomplete";
+                // A notification tells the application that the transfer's data arrived. This
+                // transfer failed on the initiator, so its data is incomplete: delivering the
+                // notification would make a partial transfer look complete. Its writes have all
+                // landed or failed by now (the initiator reports the error only once every
+                // request of the transfer has completed), so the entry is dropped; the
+                // application learns of the failure from the initiator's own error handling.
+                NIXL_ERROR << "Dropping the notification for notif_xfer_id="
+                           << it->second.notif_xfer_id
+                           << " whose transfer failed on the initiator after "
+                           << it->second.received_completions
+                           << " writes: its data is incomplete";
+                it = pending_notifications_.erase(it);
+                continue;
             }
 
             // Reassemble combined payload from fragments
